# ShelfAware reverse proxy -- install as /etc/caddy/Caddyfile, then: systemctl reload caddy.
#
# ⚠️ THREE site addresses carry a domain name below, and a self-hosted box owns none of
# them: the two on the proxy block, and the one on the www redirect. Replace all three, or
# delete the www block if you don't want a www name -- a site block left pointing at a
# domain you don't own retries ACME forever, and would 301 your visitors to someone else's
# apex if that name ever resolved to your box. Changing only the proxy block is the mistake
# this paragraph exists to prevent.
#
# Caddy handles everything the app expects from its proxy: Let's Encrypt issuance and
# renewal, WebSocket upgrade for the Blazor circuit, and the X-Forwarded-For/-Proto
# headers Program.cs honors from a loopback proxy (HSTS, the per-IP rate limits, and
# the URLs the app generates for OAuth all key on them). Swapping in a proxy that
# omits any of that breaks the corresponding feature -- see the Nginx note in
# docs/deploy-droplet.md.
#
# Two names front the same demo box: heyreginald.com (the brand domain, registered
# 2026-09-21) and demo.shelfaware.net (the original, kept so existing links and the
# 2026-08-11 deploy keep working). Both are listed deliberately -- retiring the old
# one is a separate decision, and dropping it here would break it silently.
#
# DNS FIRST, RELOAD SECOND. Every address here gets its own certificate, and issuance
# needs that name's DNS record already pointing at this droplet -- gray-cloud/DNS-only if
# the zone is on Cloudflare. A name whose DNS isn't ready doesn't take the others down,
# Caddy retries it in the background, but it serves nothing until the retry succeeds.
# (Site-block order itself is irrelevant to Caddy; it matches on host specificity.)
heyreginald.com, demo.shelfaware.net {
	reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:5000
}

# www is a redirect, not a second front door, so nobody bookmarks or links the www form.
# The box still answers on both names above, so the Host the app sees -- and therefore the
# host in the links it builds -- is whichever of those two the visitor arrived on.
www.heyreginald.com {
	redir https://heyreginald.com{uri} permanent
}
